- [1. Fundamentally, **ἀλάβαστρον** denotes an **alabaster flask**, especially a smooth vessel used for perfume or ointment. In the supplied technical passages, that basic sense develops in three main directions: first, the **pharmacological container** for aromatic substances; second, the **stone/material itself**, valued for its cold, dense, scent-preserving properties and then used as a **medicinal ingredient**; and third, in alchemy, a **coded or symbolic white mineral/substance**, sometimes also an image for the purified white vessel or body. For semantic isolation here, the relevant field excludes the geographical and metrological occurrences and keeps the medical, pharmacological, and alchemical uses. I also include the close technical derivatives **ἀλαβαστρίτης** and **ἀλαβαστροειδής**, because they make the specialized sense explicit.](./tools-texts.md#term-1-fundamentally-alabastron-denotes-an-alabaster-flask-especially-a-smooth-vessel-used-for-perfume-or-ointment-in-the-supplied-technical-passages-that-basic-sense-develops-in-three-main-directions-first-the-pharmacological-container-for-aromatic-substances-second-the-stone-material-itself-valued-for-its-cold-dense-scent-preserving-properties-and-then-used-as-a-medicinal-ingredient-and-third-in-alchemy-a-coded-or-symbolic-white-mineral-substance-sometimes-also-an-image-for-the-purified-white-vessel-or-body-for-semantic-isolation-here-the-relevant-field-excludes-the-geographical-and-metrological-occurrences-and-keeps-the-medical-pharmacological-and-alchemical-uses-i-also-include-the-close-technical-derivatives-alabastrites-and-alabastroeides-because-they-make-the-specialized-sense-explicit)
